{"task_id": "HumanEval/26", "solution": "from typing import List, Dict\ndef remove_duplicates(numbers: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\" From a list of integers, remove all elements that occur more than once.\n    Keep order of elements left the same as in the input.\n    >>> remove_duplicates([1, 2, 3, 2, 4])\n    [1, 3, 4]\n    \"\"\"\n    # Compute frequencies of all numbers in the list.\n    counts: Dict[int, int] = {}\n    for x in numbers:\n        counts[x] = counts.get(x, 0) + 1\n\n    # Build the result list by including only elements that appeared exactly once,\n    # preserving their original order.\n    result: List[int] = []\n    for x in numbers:\n        if counts.get(x, 0) == 1:\n            result.append(x)\n\n    return result"}
